selves a partially built practical  set was built so willem and tom had a  sense of where they were cg managed to  bring the environment to life as well as  to hide all the safety measures in place  for the actors like harnesses that  allowed them to fight full out it was  the most incredible experience of my  career number nine  there were a thousand different versions  for just one moment when the claw was  coming down the no way home team wanted  to make sure they did it right cg was  the name of the game when we first meet  doc ock from d-aging alfred molina in  every single shot to every one of his  tentacles molina spent about 90 of his  time on set in a harness meanwhile  another percentage of his time was spent  standing on a platform and since that  body language didn't make sense for what  was being portrayed molina's body was  usually fully digitally replaced from  the neck down highly detailed  pre-visuals were vital to make before  filming what would end up being tom  running around in a mocap suit  performing all his stunts while molina  let his cg arms do all the heavy lifting  making small efforts where he needed to  for the camera we always needed to keep  realism and weight and speed and you  know action going number ten it's iconic  for a reason watching spider-man soar  through the sky like a flying squirrel  only to land perfectly is thanks to a  ton of work from the special effects  team tom did the stunts himself with the  help of a harness and practically built  sets but all the original footage would  end up being replaced through a process  that involved mocking up the full images  of every frame of what tom was doing  digitally whenever the iron spider-man  suit was meant to be used the team had a  physical bust made out of metal that  would be brought onto the camera to see  how the light would react with it so  they could bring the most authentic  visuals possible to the cg suit  number 11.  they seriously made it rain  seriously cg played a big part in the  background in establishing the weather  but one thing it did not do was create  all that rain the special effects team  made it poor rain in the studio so  holland could really feel the vibe of  this heartbreaking scene talk about  pathetic fallacy not a dry eye or tom in  the house  number 12. the building itself was  looking pretty rough green goblin and  peter really did a number on their  surroundings and each other with  hand-to-hand combat the two actors did  themselves in studio letting cgi compose  the rest of the settings so they could  keep the action high the team was able  to safely pull off moments that saw  actors going straight out of windows  with the help of harnesses that were  erased in post we'd never have guessed  this intense moment wasn't totally  authentic but the set they built for the  actors really was a perfect base for the  editing team to then create one of the  most realistic and dramatic looking  shots  it was fun it was a lot of fun and the  stunts is something i've always really  enjoyed number 13  every detail counts  cars on the road signs  the cg is subtle but key for nailing all  the details digital cars filled in  spaces needed in the aerial shots while  signs were actually modified to say  different things in this case making  sure the sign said airport since it was  an important part of the plot this kind  of thought is part of what makes this  movie so special when peter gets to jump  on the car just a little bit of cg was  used to hide the wires until a whole lot  of cg came into play to conceal him in  the iron spider suit  number 14 zendaya's brave face was  working hard to pull off these stunts  from freaking out on top of a bridge  which fortunately wasn't so terrifying  for the actress cg taking care of the  terrifyingly high backdrop two swinging  through the studio with a harness yes  but mainly trusting tom to be in control  well that took some guts the special  effects team reflected all the terror of  really doing the stunts and more  bringing the appropriate settings to the  screen while disguising the safety rigs  for the actors  and we did it and it was amazing and i'm  proud of myself for doing it you dropped  100 feet we did it  number 15.  settings aren't always what they seem to  be much of the time the team wasn't  necessarily on location but they  constructed a makeshift version to work  with like the steps and door frame built  in studio only to be completed in post  by what's called set extension in a  sense it's easier to create the world  rather than shoot it in new york every  detail from the way the light hits  floating leaves to some of the people in  the background are courtesy of our pal  cgi  without cg many of these scenes wouldn't  have been possible in fact only about 80  shots in the entire movie didn't use vfx  in some way what cgi detail were you  most surprised by
 

